From 990acfacd1f83342501e0a41bfd2e04bfea250b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clifford Swartz <cliffordswartz1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:50:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 37/37] hw/misc: EDBG data gateway (DGI) with its host protocol

The MC00 Curiosity Pro's debugger data gateway, both sides. Toward the
host, the DGI command protocol on a chardev (-M ...,dgi=<chardev>): the
bytes a debugger exchanges on its USB DGI endpoints (sign on, version,
interface list, mode, enable, status, configuration, send, poll),
checked against an nEDBG for sign on, version, list, configuration and
status. Toward the target, an I2C target at 0x28 (SERCOM2), an SPI
target on SERCOM1 with PA17 as its slave select, and GPIO0-3 on PA10,
PA11, PA20, PA21, each feeding its interface while the host has it on;
GPIO records carry timestamps of the 2 MHz timestamp clock (record
format still to be compared with a debugger's).

hw/gpio: mchp_port_watch(), any number of observers of a pad's level
(the DGI's GPIO monitor, later a logic analyzer). hw/char: SERCOM SPI
reads MISO open (all ones) while the bus's only devices are DGI targets
that are not taking part.

Peripheral Pretender: AI-assisted; not for submission to upstream QEMU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
